 This is a local access lock. It does not encrypt the codeplug or protect memory from access outside the running
 firmware, such as the hardware bootloader. Keep your PIN somewhere you can recover it.
 
+The **CPS read PIN** is a separate, optional six-digit password. Set it under **Settings → My radio → Set or change CPS read PIN**, even if startup protection is off. The web editor asks for it on each **Read from radio**, over the programming cable. The read password authorizes only codeplug reads. For writing, backups or older software, use **Unlock or relock programming** on the radio, then relock after use. **Remove CPS read PIN** requires the existing read PIN. Both PINs are off on a fresh radio.
